      "updated_at": "2026-09-05T14:12:14Z",
      "body": "Hi! I’d like to work on this issue.\n\nI reviewed the current Compare entry points in `src/lib/ui/CompareFloatingButton.svelte` and `src/routes/products/[barcode]/ProductHeader.svelte`. Both currently use `@iconify-svelte/mdi/compare` at `h-5 w-5`.\n\nMy proposal is to replace that icon consistently in both places with `@iconify-svelte/mdi/swap-horizontal`. The two opposing horizontal arrows communicate comparing two items side-by-side more directly than the current split-style compare glyph, while staying within the project’s existing MDI/Iconify dependency. I would keep the existing Compare text, `title`, and `aria-label` behavior unchanged, and verify the icon at the current mobile and desktop sizes.\n\nIf this direction looks good, could I be assigned #1660 before I start the implementation?\n\n**AI usage disclosure:** I’m using ChatGPT (GPT-5.6 Sol) as a primary coding assistant and Google Antigravity CLI with Gemini 3.1 Pro as a read-only second reviewer. I will review and test all changes myself and take responsibility for the submitted code.\n",
